  "notes": "{揃|そろ}える means to arrange neatly or gather together.\n\nTRANSITIVITY PAIR:\n- {揃|そろ}える (transitive): to arrange, gather\n- ⟦{揃|そろ}う→揃う：01953_sorou⟧ (intransitive): to be complete, be aligned\n\nCOMMON USES:\n- ⟦{靴|くつ}→靴：00725_kutsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{揃|そろ}える: to arrange shoes neatly\n- ⟦{材料|ざいりょう}→材料：02831_zairyou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{揃|そろ}える: to gather ingredients\n- ⟦{足並|あしな}み→足並み：27780_ashinami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{揃|そろ}える: to get in step\n- ⟦{息|いき}→息：02176_iki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{揃|そろ}える: to synchronize breathing\n- ⟦{条件|じょうけん}→条件：03285_jouken⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{揃|そろ}える: to meet all conditions\n\nCONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- {揃|そろ}えない (negative)\n- {揃|そろ}えて (te-form)\n- {揃|そろ}えた (past)\n\nCULTURE:\nArranging shoes neatly when entering a home is important Japanese etiquette.",
